S2DEX sprites through the 2D matrix are drawn (warecomp STATUS.md round 19).

G_OBJ_MOVEMEM (gSPObjMatrix, gSPObjSubMatrix) wasn't handled, and
G_OBJ_SPRITE / G_OBJ_LDTX_SPRITE / G_OBJ_LDTX_RECT_R loaded their texture
and drew nothing (TODOs). Worms Armageddon draws its rotating sprites that
way (func_8000762C: a rotation matrix, then G_OBJ_LDTX_SPRITE), among them
the air strike's target cursor, which didn't show at all.

The matrix is kept; a matrix sprite is drawn as an upright rectangle the
size the matrix scales it to, centred where the matrix puts its centre (the
rotation itself is left out, as RT64's rectangles are axis-aligned); a
RECTANGLE_R through the matrix's translation and base scale.

